        "Content": "Enjoying a superb position in a quiet and established enclave, 9 Darley Street is a charming two-bedroom townhouse that combines period character with a comfortable, contemporary layout.\r\n\r\nBehind its attractive brick façade, this appealing home offers well-proportioned accommodation arranged over two floors, with a particularly generous living room, extended kitchen and two bedrooms upstairs. The property retains a number of attractive period features, including original timber flooring, a fireplace, while a number of important modern upgrades have been carried out.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation is immediately welcoming, with an entrance porch leading into the spacious living room. Measuring approximately 4.16m x 5.62m, this is an excellent main reception space with built-in storage and shelving, providing a comfortable setting for both relaxing and entertaining.\r\n\r\nTo the rear, the kitchen extension provides a practical modern workspace with direct connection to the outdoor area. A bathroom completes the ground floor. Upstairs, there are two well-proportioned bedrooms. The bedrooms benefit from excellent natural light, with the layout providing attractive dual-aspect accommodation to the front and rear.\r\n\r\nWhether as a first home, city base or investment, 9 Darley Street offers the increasingly sought-after combination of period character, manageable proportions, excellent connectivity and a convenient Dublin 6 location.\r\n\r\nHarold’s Cross has developed into one of Dublin’s most popular inner-suburban neighbourhoods, retaining its traditional village character while benefiting from an increasingly vibrant selection of independent cafés, restaurants, shops and local businesses.\r\n\r\nThe property is particularly well positioned for enjoying the Grand Canal, with the canal-side route providing an attractive setting for walking, running and cycling towards Portobello and the city. Harold’s Cross Park is another excellent local amenity, with its historic green, playground and café.\r\n\r\nFor everyday convenience, Harold’s Cross Road offers a broad selection of shops and services, while Rathmines, Ranelagh, Portobello and Camden Street are all within easy reach. The local food and coffee scene includes established favourites alongside newer independent operators, with cafés, restaurants, bakeries and pubs all contributing to the area's strong village atmosphere.\r\n\r\nThere are a host of bus routes within short walking distance from the front door, while the Luas Green Line can be accessed via Charlemont/Ranelagh, providing direct connection to the city centre, or out towards Sandyford, etc. For cyclists and walkers, the property's proximity to the canal provides a particularly attractive alternative, while the city centre, Portobello and Camden Street are all readily accessible.\r\n\r\nLocal area\r\nSchools: St Clare's, Harold's Cross Etns, St. Louis, St. Mary's College, St. Louis, Rathmines College and many more nearby\r\nBus routes (within 10 mins): 9, 16, 16d, 49, 54a, F1, F2 & F3\r\nLuas: Charlemont stop (c. 15-minutes by foot)\r\n\r\nProperty features\r\nc. 58 sq. m. (624 sq. ft.)\r\nGFCH\r\nF – BER rating\r\nPermit parking\r\nYear of construction: c. 1900"
      },
